# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/)
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org).

## [v0.1.0-beta] 2026-11-02

### Added

This is a Beta release. I have tested it on my machine but have not had a chance to have other examiners test it yet.

Collection and preservation features are complete, but reporting features are likely to change in future versions.

There are 2 binaries, `apple-message-forensics` is for Apple Silicon and `apple-message-forensics-macos-intel` is for Macs running Intel chips.

See the Install section of the README if you don't know how to use 7zip.

Verify the hash with `sha256sum apple-message-forensics_v0.1.0.7z`.

### Known Limitations

#### Cellebrite Reporting

- The Address Book migration from MacOS to iOS format does not copy all Address Book data, but only the following
  - Name
  - Emails
  - Phone Numbers

My intent behind collecting the Address Book is to join Contact Names to message handles.

